A bridged @Observable reports each read and write from whichever thread makes it, and the provenance hook fed them into the animation stack and read cursor, which belong to the main actor: a model read on a background thread raced the main thread's appends and trapped in Array's copy. The hook now records the thread the first withAnimation scope runs on and ignores bridged accesses on any other, where no scope can be open and no modifier's arguments are being read.

